scope: "The BINDABLE-ORDER / VISIBILITY container (`ordered_stack`, `OrderedFlowContainer`) — a flex flow whose child LAYOUT ORDER and SHOWN-SET are bound to ComposeBus state namespaces, so a publish reorders / hides / shows the children and the container REFLOWS. A CAPTURE of a primitive that is already BUILT, TESTED (9 tests) and IN PRODUCTION (the console collaboration rail), authored because seven references across the corpus cite [SPEC:CXC-ORDER] and no document carrying that id has ever existed. Covers: the `_flow_children()` layout-order hook it overrides ([CXC-R-ENGINE-LAYOUT]); the strict-additive-superset/zero-diff identity path; the `state_namespace` order+shown-set payload grammar (list OR `{order, hidden, visible}` dict); the SEPARATE `visibility_namespace` shown-set source and the order/visibility UNCOUPLING invariant that [SPEC:CXC-IC-LAUNCH]'s pane swap depends on; reversibility (the declared child list is never mutated, so draw z-order and hit-test stay declared); the hot-add hook; change-gated damage-scoped redraw; the `.compose.yaml` declaration surface; and the divergences between the de-facto docstring spec and the actual code, FLAGGED not redesigned."
