## 4. Acceptance — the evidence this capture rests on

### [CXC-ORD-VERIFY] Two-tier verdicts — each captured claim traced to its test, and the gaps named

- definition: every claim in this document is traceable to a code line and, where covered, to one of the 9 tests in `python/tests/render/test_ordered_container.py`. Rows whose `verify.machine` cell says NO DIRECT TEST are honest coverage gaps in the BUILT artifact, recorded here rather than papered over — a `built` claim without a verification handle reads as "spec'd, unverified" ([CAP-MODEL-FACETS] / [SBR-TRUST]).

| ID | Captured claim | verify.machine | verify.human (glass) |
|----|----------------|----------------|----------------------|
| ORD-C1 | Zero-diff identity: no state published → pixel-identical to `stack` ([CXC-ORD-SUPERSET]) | `test_default_layout_is_byte_identical_to_stack` — pixel compare at `tolerance=0, max_diff_ratio=0.0` plus exact per-child rect equality | on glass: the console rail after the `stack`→`ordered_stack` conversion looks unchanged until something publishes |
| ORD-C2 | A LIST payload pure-reorders and never touches visibility ([CXC-ORD-ORDER-STATE]) | `test_list_state_reorders` — laid order follows the list; all children still `visible` | on glass: cards move; none disappear |
| ORD-C3 | A `{order, hidden}` dict reorders AND hides AND the flow COMPACTS ([CXC-ORD-SHOWN-SET]) | `test_dict_state_reorders_and_hides_and_compacts` — `b.visible is False`, laid order `["a","c"]`, and `yc == ya + CARD_H + GAP` (no hole) | on glass: the hidden card leaves no gap — the rail closes up |
| ORD-C4 | Visibility is STICKY across a bare reorder; clearing restores ([CXC-ORD-ORDER-STATE]) | `test_visibility_is_sticky_until_changed` — a reorder after a hide does not un-hide; `{"hidden": []}` restores all three | on glass: reordering a rail with a hidden card does not resurrect it |
| ORD-C5 | `visible` is an allow-list ([CXC-ORD-SHOWN-SET]) | `test_visible_allowlist_shows_only_listed` — only listed ids shown, in declared relative order | on glass: an allow-list publish leaves exactly the named cards |
| ORD-C6 | `visibility_namespace` is a genuinely separate second source, accepting a hidden-list OR a `{id: bool}` shown-map ([CXC-ORD-VIS-NAMESPACE]) | `test_separate_visibility_namespace` (both payload shapes) + `test_parser_builds_ordered_stack_and_subscribes` (both namespaces subscribed for the one widget) | on glass ([SPEC:CXC-IC-LAUNCH]): the pane swaps while a concurrent rail reorder survives — neither writer stomps the other |
| ORD-C7 | Reversibility: `self.children` is never mutated; draw/hit-test stay declared ([CXC-ORD-REVERSIBLE]) | `test_declared_child_list_is_never_mutated` — declared list unchanged after reorder+hide; clearing restores the laid order | on glass: overlapping children keep their stacking through a reorder (no flicker) |
| ORD-C8 | Damage is change-gated and scoped ([CXC-ORD-DAMAGE]) | `test_reflow_requests_redraw_on_change` — a real change dirties, an identical republish does not. **PARTIAL**: the bus de-dupes identical publishes (`namespace.py:82`), so the gate's own no-op path (a different payload shape → same effective state) is inspection-only | on glass: driving the rail does not re-raster the whole console |
| ORD-C9 | Hot-add integrates with an active order/allow-list ([CXC-ORD-HOT-ADD]) | **NO DIRECT TEST of `register_added_child`'s three effects.** Exercised indirectly by `test_hot_add.py` (its parent is an `ordered_stack`) and `test_console_app_surfaces.py::test_s4_hot_add_mounts_into_running_rail_and_binds` | on glass: a widget dropped into a rail under an active allow-list appears immediately (`drive_ordered_reflow.py` is the visual driver) |
| ORD-C10 | The parser builds all three type spellings and both namespace keys ([CXC-ORD-DECLARE]) | `test_parser_builds_ordered_stack_and_subscribes` covers `ordered_stack` + both keys. **NO TEST** covers the `orderedstack` / `flow_stack` spellings or the `order_namespace` alias (zero usages in the repo) | n/a (structural) |
| ORD-C11 | A malformed payload is tolerated ([CXC-ORD-ORDER-STATE]) | **NO TEST.** Inspection: a scalar/string payload matches no branch in `apply_order_state` and is a silent no-op ([CXC-ORD-OPEN] O8) | n/a (structural) |
| ORD-C12 | Duplicate-id children ([CXC-ORD-CONTAINER] step 2) | **NO TEST.** Inspection: with any state active only the FIRST child of a duplicated id lays out ([CXC-ORD-OPEN] O4) | n/a (structural) |

- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-ORDER]

