**Version**: 0.1
**Created**: 2026-08-10
**Updated**: 2026-08-10 (v0.1) — INITIAL CAPTURE of a primitive that was built, tested and shipped without a spec. Authored from `python/composeio/render/engine/layout.py:347-517` (+ the `_flow_children()` base hook at `:137-147`), `parser.py:1473-1535`, `runtime.py:946-953`, the 9 tests in `python/tests/render/test_ordered_container.py`, and the production wiring at `intelligence/console/console.compose.yaml:1019-1022` / `:1507-1523`. Closes the dangling `uses:`/`USES` edges carried by [CXC-ICL-PANE-SWAP] and [SPEC:CXC-IC-LAUNCH] (spec 55 was NOT edited — it is being landed concurrently). Four invariants captured: [CXC-ORD-SUPERSET] (zero-diff identity path), [CXC-ORD-VIS-NAMESPACE] (order/visibility uncoupling — the property the pane swap depends on), [CXC-ORD-REVERSIBLE] (the declared child list is never mutated), [CXC-ORD-DAMAGE] (change-gated, scoped redraw). Thirteen divergences between the de-facto docstring spec and the actual code are FLAGGED in [CXC-ORD-OPEN] and deliberately NOT corrected in the prose — notably the `direction` default (`column` vs `stack`'s `row`, which qualifies the literal zero-diff claim), the `hidden`-beats-`visible` resolution order (the docstring says "last key wins"), duplicate-id child loss under any active state, and the three co-owners of `child.visible`.
**Status**: RATIFY-READY (capture of built behaviour). The behavioural content is not a proposal — it is a transcription of running code, each claim traced to a line and, where covered, to a test. What the architect ratifies is (a) that this document is the intended home of [SPEC:CXC-ORDER], (b) the [CAP-BINDABLE-ORDER] maturity/tier calls, and (c) the disposition of the thirteen open items in [CXC-ORD-OPEN] — each of which, if actioned, is a CODE change that this document is then updated to match. NEXT: add [CAP-BINDABLE-ORDER] to [CAP-MAP]'s `see-also` roster in 49; close the ORD-C9/C10/C11/C12 test gaps if the architect wants the `built` claim fully handled; decide O1 (the `direction` default) before any further `stack`→`ordered_stack` conversion.
